{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 2 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 2 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_4>\nfrom __future__ import print_function\n\ntab1 = {}\ntab2 = {}\n\ndef num1(n):\n    if n < 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n < 2:\n        return 1\n    else:\n        if n not in tab1:\n            r = 0\n            i = 0\n            while i < n:\n                r += num1(i) * num1(n - 1 - i)\n                i += 1\n            tab1[n] = r\n        return tab1[n]\n    return tab1[n]\n\ndef num2(n, h):\n    if n < 0 or h <= 0 or n >= 2 ** (h - 1):\n        return 0\n    elif n < 2:\n        return 1\n    elif n < h:\n        return num1(n)\n    else:\n        if (n, h) not in tab2:\n            r = 0\n            i = 0\n            while i < n:\n                r += num2(i, h - 1) * num2(n - 1 - i, h - 1)\n                i += 1\n            tab2[(n, h)] = r\n        return tab2[(n, h)]\n    return tab2[(n, h)]\n\n\nline = raw_input()\nparts = line.split()\nn = int(parts[0])\nh = int(parts[1])\nprint num1(n) - num2(n, h)\n</your_rewritten_code_4>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <map>\n#include <string>\n#include <sstream>\n\nstd::map<long long, long long> tab1;\nstd::map<std::pair<long long, long long>, long long> tab2;\n\nlong long num1(long long n) {\n    if (n < 0) {\n        return 0;\n    } else if (n < 2) {\n        return 1;\n    } else {\n        if (tab1.find(n) == tab1.end()) {\n            long long r = 0;\n            long long i = 0;\n            while (i < n) {\n                r += num1(i) * num1(n - 1 - i);\n                i += 1;\n            }\n            tab1[n] = r;\n        }\n        return tab1[n];\n    }\n}\n\nlong long num2(long long n, long long h) {\n    if (n < 0 || h <= 0 || n >= (1LL << (h - 1))) {\n        return 0;\n    } else if (n < 2) {\n        return 1;\n    } else if (n < h) {\n        return num1(n);\n    } else {\n        std::pair<long long, long long> key = std::make_pair(n, h);\n        if (tab2.find(key) == tab2.end()) {\n            long long r = 0;\n            long long i = 0;\n            while (i < n) {\n                r += num2(i, h - 1) * num2(n - 1 - i, h - 1);\n                i += 1;\n            }\n            tab2[key] = r;\n        }\n        return tab2[key];\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    std::string line;\n    std::getline(std::cin, line);\n    std::istringstream iss(line);\n    long long n, h;\n    iss >> n >> h;\n    std::cout << num1(n) - num2(n, h) << std::endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00013028726971242577, -9.298280929215252e-06, -9.536738616588991e-07, -8.272782724816352e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.00010871296399272978, -5.960462772236497e-07, -9.536738616588991e-07, 0.0, -0.03674608841538429, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.00038020533975213766, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.23926953971385956, -9.298280929215252e-06, -1.680836794548668e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0311291366815567, -0.5231319665908813, -0.011222336441278458